$ bof3 assets export bogus a
[exit 2]
bof3 assets: export has no "bogus" direction; run `bof3 assets export --help` for texture, tim, palette, terrain, vag, vab, sequence, seq, sep, message, script, strings, characters, character-bank and sprite-sheet

$ bof3 assets export
[exit 2]
bof3 assets: export needs a kind, for example texture; run `bof3 assets export --help`

$ bof3 assets export script bank.emi0
[exit 0]
wrote bank.txt

; A script bank: one animation stream per record. Actor_BeginScript (exe/slus_004_22@0x8014D6DC)
; points an actor at a record and Actor_SeekScript (exe/slus_004_22@0x8014D910) plays it.
; show: stage a frame for its ticks (Actor_StageAnimStep; a tick is 33.4 ms, 0 lasts 256).
; jump: continue at a step (Actor_StepAnimLoop, Actor_StepAnimOnce). Labels name the steps jumps reach.
bof3-script 1

section 0
slots 0

record 0
    show frame 0 ticks 4    ; step 0, 133 ms
s1:
    show frame 1 ticks 6    ; step 1, 200 ms
    jump s1    ; step 2
frame 0
    cell shape 5 x -8 y -16 u 0 v 0
frame 1
    cell shape 5 flip x -8 y -16 u 16 v 0
pad 00 00

$ bof3 assets import script bank.txt --payload bank.emi0 -o back.emi0
[exit 0]
wrote back.emi0

$ bof3 assets import script bank.txt
[exit 2]
bof3 assets: import script needs --payload, the bank it was exported from; run `bof3 assets import script --help`

$ bof3 assets import strings stub.bin
[exit 2]
bof3 assets: import strings needs --payload, the file it was exported from; run `bof3 assets import strings --help`

$ bof3 assets import encounters stub.bin
[exit 2]
bof3 assets: import encounters needs --base, the stored block; run `bof3 assets import encounters --help`

$ bof3 assets export vag stub.bin stub.bin
[exit 2]
bof3 assets: export vag needs --index, the VAG's number in the bank; run `bof3 assets export vag --help`

$ bof3 assets export vag stub.bin
[exit 2]
bof3 assets: export vag needs a header (.vh) and a body (.vb) file; run `bof3 assets export vag --help`

$ bof3 assets export texture stub.bin
[exit 2]
bof3 assets: export texture needs --load-arg, the entry's load address; run `bof3 assets export texture --help`

$ bof3 assets export texture stub.bin --load-arg zz
[exit 2]
bof3 assets: --load-arg needs a number, not "zz"; run `bof3 assets export texture --help`

$ bof3 assets import emi stub.bin --entry oops
[exit 2]
bof3 assets: --entry needs INDEX=FILE, not "oops"; run `bof3 assets import emi --help`

$ bof3 assets import sequence stub.bin
[exit 2]
bof3 assets: "stub.bin" needs FILE:ID; run `bof3 assets import sequence --help`

$ bof3 assets import disc game.cue
[exit 2]
bof3 assets: import disc needs -o DIR, a new directory for the patched disc; run `bof3 assets import disc --help`

$ bof3 assets tables
[exit 2]
bof3 assets: tables needs the stored bytes of GAME.EMI entry 0; run `bof3 assets tables --help`

